RUN test_stack_merge_preserves_method_and_records_outcome
ok - stack fallback delegates atomic merging to gh stack merge with methods, preflight and recorded outcome
RUN test_stack_participant_locks_and_authority
ok - stack holds serialize through dispatch and every owned participant receives matching authority before unlock
RUN test_stack_collision_is_rechecked_before_dispatch
ok - stack dispatch refuses newly colliding and unreadable numeric targets
RUN test_stack_failure_before_submission_publishes_nothing
ok - pre-submission and unproven stack failures publish neither authority nor uncertainty
RUN test_stack_failure_reconciles_once_for_all_participants
ok - stack errors reconcile landed, unmerged and unreadable outcomes once for every owned participant
RUN test_orphan_registration_refuses_worker_replacement
ok - explicit and flagless orphan registration preserve replacement workers without publishing stale polls
RUN test_orphan_merge_retains_context_under_control
ok - explicit orphan merges retain binding and task control across registration, re-recording and stack lock reacquisition
RUN test_orphan_identity_is_fixed_at_publication
ok - ordinary recording and prior-merged helper entry preserve the stored orphan identity
RUN test_registration_serializes_orphan_discovery
ok - orphan and ordinary registration serialize ownership in both orders
RUN test_registration_waits_for_stack_dispatch
ok - held unbound tasks cannot publish a PR binding during stack dispatch
RUN test_busy_stack_participant_refuses_without_deadlock
ok - busy stack participants refuse and release ownership without a control/publication deadlock
RUN test_stack_extra_aliases_refuse
ok - stack fallback rejects unrequired public method and confirmation aliases
RUN test_orphan_lifecycle
ok - forge-only records have current state, valid inventory and cleanup without worker or backlog fields
RUN test_stack_merge_refuses_unsafe_state
ok - stack fallback refuses red, absent, changed, ambiguous, away, held and unsupported states and surfaces CLI failure
RUN test_orphan_recording_preserves_guards
ok - explicit orphan merge records the live head and outcome while retaining red, missing-check and hold guards
RUN test_orphan_never_overwrites_an_owner
ok - orphan mode requires opt-in and never replaces or bypasses an owning worker

